% spec 11 §5 gate 3: a chain B (b0 -> b1 -> b2) beside four one-shot
% events e1..e4 on their own tokens — resource-DISJOINT by construction
% (no atom of one is read or written by the other). Blocking an e-event
% can change P(b2) only through a global event-count horizon (they
% compete for steps), never through causation: @N cone steps must read
% PN = 0, a short global N leaks.
catalog disjoint-chains 1.
provenance hand "spec 11 bias fixture" "2026-10-08".
layers (story).
stages (go).
namespace w produce (story).
pred b0 : w.
pred b1 : w.
pred b2 : w.
pred x1 : w.
pred x2 : w.
pred x3 : w.
pred x4 : w.
pred y : w.
stage go {
  %% the chain's first link.
  b_one [story] : b0 -o b1.
  %% the chain's second link.
  b_two [story] : b1 -o b2.
  %% noise, on its own token.
  e1 [story] : x1 -o y.
  %% noise, on its own token.
  e2 [story] : x2 -o y.
  %% noise, on its own token.
  e3 [story] : x3 -o y.
  %% noise, on its own token.
  e4 [story] : x4 -o y.
}
#init b0 1
#init x1 1
#init x2 1
#init x3 1
#init x4 1
#steps 6
